  "question": {
    "text": "Area of the region bounded by the curve $y=e^x$ and lines $x=0$ and $y=e$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$e-1$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\int_1^e \\ln (e+1-y) d y$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$e-\\int_0^1 e^x d x$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\int_1^e \\ln y d y$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Shaded area $=e-\\left(\\int_0^1 e^x d x\\right)=1$\nAlso, $\\quad \\int_1^e \\ln (e+1-y) d y$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0015_73e0e8417ed9.png\"><br>\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\int_e^q \\ln t(-d t) \\\\\n& \\text { [put } e+1-y=t \\Rightarrow-d y=d t \\text { ] } \\\\\n& =\\int_1^e \\ln t d t=\\int_1^e \\ln y d y=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
